{
  "about": "Scroll stress suite for scroll_probe.py (issues #642, #668): every Windows page and modal with a scroller, probed with three wheel cycles and two scrollbar-drag cycles against loopback fixtures. 'open' steps run through FstUia after launch (a modal's 'target' is 'dialog'); 'env' adds launch environment ({repo} is the repository root); frame intervals and each frame's UI-thread work (Rendering to the thread's next idle moment) are judged against 'thresholds', which override the defaults per page ('drag' holds limits for the scrollbar-drag passes only), and an entry whose limits exceed the defaults names its tracked jank in 'known'. Lists that would fit the window use rivals_fixture.py --stress-lists or --large-rankings.",
